config PAMIR_AI_SAM_MODULE
	tristate "Pamir AI Signal Aggregation Module (SAM) driver"
	depends on SERIAL_DEV_BUS
	help
	  Say Y here to support Pamir AI's Signal Aggregation Module (SAM)
	  for communication between the host processor and RP2040 microcontroller.
	  
	  This driver interfaces with hardware components on the CM5 device,
	  including:
	  - Button input handling via Linux input subsystem
	  - RGB LED control (up to 16 LEDs with different animation modes)
	  - Boot/shutdown notifications via Linux reboot notifier
	  - Diagnostic information and debugging
	  
	  The driver also creates a character device at /dev/pamir-sam
	  for direct userspace communication with the microcontroller.
	  
	  Debug level can be controlled with the 'debug' module parameter
	  (0=off, 1=errors, 2=info, 3=verbose).
	  
	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
	  will be called pamir-ai-sam. 